    "result_text": "Full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\nDone. I implemented customerCode de-duplication in `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- The step now injects `OwnerRepository` and computes the base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>` as before.\n- It collects all existing owners' `customerCode` values, then if the computed code collides, appends `-<n>` starting at `n=2`, incrementing until the code is unique.\n- The de-duplicated code is what gets stored, so it flows on to `AssignMembershipNumber` and the response.\n\nThis runs within the existing `govern: [ transaction ]` pipeline (it's already wired at `assignCustomerCode` in `owners.POST.yml`), and the acceptance test's guarantee \u2014 distinct owners always get distinct customer codes \u2014 holds. The full test suite is green.",
