    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a coherent, additive extension of the existing step class:\n\n- The de-duplication logic belongs in `AssignCustomerCode`. Producing a *unique* customer code is a natural extension of the step's single responsibility (assigning the code), not a second concern bolted on \u2014 the class name still describes what it does.\n- The new `OwnerRepository` dependency is injected by type as a plain parameter, exactly the idiom the codebase uses for repository-backed steps (e.g. `Save`/`Load`), so a maintainer would find it natural. Re-introducing the dependency on stored owners is inherent to the spec (collision detection needs them), and the javadoc was correctly updated to reflect that the earlier \"no longer depends on other owners\" claim no longer holds.\n- No duplication is introduced, and the method stays focused: compute base code \u2192 gather existing codes \u2192 find the smallest suffix. It reads top-to-bottom cleanly.\n- The `hash8` sub-computation remains factored into its private helper, and the mutate-in-place `@Val Owner` / `setCustomerCode` shape matches the `Apply`-style convention.\n\nNothing here rises to a structural problem worth changing.",
